.TH DWM\-MSG 1 dwm\-VERSION
.SH NAME
dwm\-msg \- send commands to dwm and read its state and events
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B dwm\-msg
.RB [ \-s
.IR socket ]
.I command
.RI [ args ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B dwm\-msg
joins its arguments into one line, sends it to dwm's IPC socket and prints
the reply, one line of JSON. It exits 1 when dwm answers
.B {"success":false,...}
or cannot be reached. After
.BR subscribe ,
it keeps printing the events, one JSON object per line, until dwm restarts or
exits.
.P
The socket is
.IR socket ,
else
.BR $DWM_SOCKET ,
else the root window property
.B _DWM_IPC_SOCKET
on
.BR $DISPLAY .
Any program that writes a line to the socket and reads one back works too,
e.g.
.BR "echo get_tasks | socat \- UNIX\-CONNECT:$DWM_SOCKET" .
.P
Several commands can be sent on one line, separated by ';'. Commands answer
.B {"success":true}
or
.BR {"success":false,"error":"..."} ;
queries answer their data.
.SH QUERIES
.TP
.B get_tree
the tree of the workspace shown on each monitor: containers with
.BR layout " (splith, splitv, stacked, tabbed), " fact " and " nodes ,
windows as in
.BR get_windows .
.TP
.B get_tasks
the tasks:
.BR num ", " name ", " focused ", " urgent ", " windows .
.TP
.B get_tags
the tags of the focused monitor in the active task:
.BR num ", " name ", " focused ", " occupied ", " urgent .
.TP
.B get_windows
every managed window:
.BR id ", " title ", " class ", " instance ", " task ", " tasknum ", " tag
(0: every tag),
.BR monitor ", " floating ", " fullscreen ", " minimized ", " urgent ", " focused .
.TP
.B get_focused
the focused window, or null.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.BR "focus left" | right | up | down
directional focus, as Mod\-arrows.
.TP
.BR "focus next" | prev
the next/previous window in the client list.
.TP
.B focus urgent
the urgent window, on any task and tag (Mod\-u).
.TP
.B focus mode_toggle
between the tiled and the floating windows.
.TP
.BI "focus id " window
that window, showing its task and tag (a minimized one is restored).
.TP
.BR "move left" | right | up | down
move the focused window, as Mod\-Shift\-arrows.
.TP
.BR "split h" | v
as Mod\-h / Mod\-v.
.TP
.BR "layout splith" | splitv | stacked | stacking | tabbed
the layout of the focused window's container (or of the workspace).
.TP
.B layout toggle split
as Mod\-e.
.TP
.BI "view " tag
show tag 1..10.
.TP
.BI "tag " tag
move the focused window to tag 1..10.
.TP
.BI "task " task
switch to a task, given by its number or its label.
.TP
.BI "movetotask " task
move the focused window to that task.
.TP
.BI "newtask " label
a new task after the active one, which becomes active.
.TP
.BI "renametask " label
rename the active task.
.TP
.B deltask
remove the active task; its windows go to the neighbouring one.
.TP
.BR "resize grow" | shrink " width" | height
as one step of resize mode.
.TP
.BR floating ", " fullscreen ", " minimize ", " kill
toggle floating / fullscreen, minimize or close the focused window.
.TP
.BR "mode resize" | move | default
enter or leave a binding mode.
.TP
.B overview
show or hide the task overview (Mod\-o).
.TP
.BI "exec " "command line"
run it with /bin/sh; the rest of the line, ';' included, is the command.
.TP
.BR restart ", " exit
restart dwm in place, or quit.
.SH EVENTS
.TP
.BI "subscribe " event ...
with
.IR event " one of " focus ", " tag ", " task ", " window ", " tree ", " mode
or
.BR all .
Each event is a line such as
.BR {"event":"focus","window":{...}} :
.B focus
(the focused window, or null),
.B tag
(as
.BR get_tags ),
.B task
(as
.BR get_tasks ),
.B window
.RB ( change ": new, close or title, and the " window ),
.B tree
(as
.BR get_tree ,
after any change of the trees) and
.B mode
.RB ( mode ": resize, move or default)."
A client that does not read its events fast enough is disconnected.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
dwm\-msg get_tree
dwm\-msg 'split v; exec st'
dwm\-msg task work
dwm\-msg subscribe focus tag
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR dwm (1)
